{{!
    @template tool_vae/chronology

    The chronology of a declaration, as a fold: its heading, then one line per act, its day then what was done (one end
    of line after the opening of the list and after each item, as the writer of the core put them).

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\chronology. The template holds no logic. Every
    value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * heading - string, the heading of the fold
    * acts - array of {date, act}: the day of an act and what was done

    Example context (json):
    {
        "heading": "Chronology",
        "acts": [
            {"date": "1 June 2026", "act": "Declared"},
            {"date": "2 June 2026", "act": "Attested"}
        ]
    }
}}
<details class="mb-2"><summary>{{heading}}</summary><ul class="tool-vae-chronology">
{{#acts}}<li><span class="text-muted">{{date}}</span> - {{act}}</li>
{{/acts}}</ul></details>
